==English==

===Etymology===
Yiddish [[shtup#Yiddish|shtup]], perhaps from German [[stupsen]] ‘nudge’, or possibly German [[stopfen]] 'stuff'.  
In 2008 the term was brought into common use  by Dr Reddy (aka Terminator); particularly during ward rounds. Dr Reddy is the author of the 'shtup protocol'. The term has since taken off around parts of Sydney, Australia.

